<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Vila</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port Vila is a port town on the island of Efate and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>. In 1889 French and other settlers there declared the short-lived commune of Franceville, independent of both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It later became the seat of the Anglo-French Condominium of the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> and, from 1980, of independent Vanuatu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-vila.jpg" alt="Port Vila" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phillip Capper from Wellington, New Zealand · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Vila_aerial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
